================================================================================
HEADLINE RESULT  [PHASE 1 ONLY -- SUPERSEDED, see "PHASE 2 (with key)" below]
================================================================================
The preflight is NOT the problem. All three REST preflights succeed and return
a correct Access-Control-Allow-Origin.

The ACTUAL response is the problem. When an Authorization header is present,
the real POST response from api.openai.com carries NO Access-Control-Allow-Origin
header at all, so the browser discards it before page JS can see it. Chromium
names the failure exactly: corsError = MissingAllowOriginHeader.

The same POST WITHOUT an Authorization header returns
Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * and is fully readable. So the stripping is tied
to the authenticated request path, which is precisely the BYOK path.

